{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-16 22:14:27 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-17 05:14:27 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nThe independent static second traversal is complete: **155 of 155 fixtures passed**, with both reopened row closures and their recorded admission coordinates checked. All fixture IDs and row counts match the r9e outcomes. The focused tests passed **5 tests / 23 assertions**, and kondo reported zero errors and warnings.\n\nThe C-lane measurements, bounds declaration, tagged verification, and publication artifacts remain incomplete. The one pre-declaration tagged pilot reported previously remains recorded honestly; no further tagged fixture was run. The store remains uncommitted, and no commit was made.\n\nThe [findings](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1/collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md) and [row-recheck outcomes](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1/collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-row-recheck.edn) are in the worktree mirror.\n\nThe sequencing question remains: **may the tagged C-lane measurements run before the declaration as an explicit exception, or must bounds be declared first?** The repeated brief requires measurements first while also binding design §6.3, which says bounds precede any tagged run."}}
